{"severity":"error","file":"errors/duplicate_binder_4.march","start_line":6,"start_col":10,"end_line":6,"end_col":11,"message":"`a` is bound twice in the same parameter list or pattern.","code":"duplicate_binder","fix":null,"labels":[{"file":"errors/duplicate_binder_4.march","start_line":6,"start_col":7,"end_line":6,"end_col":8,"message":"first bound here"}],"notes":["A parameter list or a pattern binds each name once, so there is no single value this name could refer to.","Rename one of them, or write `_` for an argument you don't use. To require two values to be equal, bind two names and compare them in a `when` guard: `(a, a2) when a == a2 -> …`."]}
